    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **68 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner response.\n\n**What `ownerSegment` returns** \u2014 `<TIER>_<AREA>`, one of `PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`:\n- **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel \u2265 3`, else `STANDARD`\n- **AREA**: `METRO` when locality is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`\n\n**Changes** (following the existing `ageBand` pattern):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` property to the `Owner` schema as a read-only string enum with the four allowed values (generates `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`).\n\n2. **`OwnerSegments.java`** (new helper) \u2014 computes the segment. It reads `membershipLevel` (the stored value, falling back to `MembershipLevels.of(owner)` when absent, exactly as the mapper's `membershipLevel` field does) and the locality via `Localities.region(owner)`, treating anything other than `\"UNKNOWN\"` as METRO.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired the new field with a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression delegating to `OwnerSegments.of(owner)`.\n\nBoth new tests pass: a known-region STANDARD owner \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, and an unknown-city STANDARD owner \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`.",
